WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Functional Anatomy of the Infraspinatus & Posterior Rotator Cuff.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The infraspinatus is a thick triangular rotator cuff muscle occupying the infraspinous fossa of the scapula.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:10.000
It originates from the medial two-thirds of the infraspinous fossa and inserts onto the middle facet of the greater tubercle of the humerus.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Innervated by the suprascapular nerve (roots C5, C6) passing through the spinoglenoid notch.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:57.000
Primary action: Powerful lateral (external) rotation of the glenohumeral joint and stabilization of the humeral head in the glenoid cavity.
